    "key_facts": "Each fact is a list of alternatives; a fact is found when any alternative occurs in the normalised text. Used for Answer Correctness (in Piper's answer) and Context Recall (in Piper's retrieved passages).",
    "normalisation": "lower case, accents stripped, '¼' -> '1/4', thousands separators removed (24 000 / 24,000 -> 24000), 'N x M' -> 'NxM', whitespace collapsed.",
    "expected_tools": "Every entry must be matched by at least one call whose tool is in 'names'. 'args' is checked against the call of names[0] only (an alternative tool is accepted for selection but its arguments are not scored).",
    "args_matchers": "string = loose equals (lower case, accents and non-alphanumerics removed); number = equals; {contains}; {oneOf: [...]}; {includesAny: [...]} for list parameters; {present: true}; any matcher object may add allowMissing: true.",
    "optional_tools": "Calls to these tools never count against exact-set match.",
    "forbidden_tools": "Calling any of these is a violation. 'expect_no_tools': true forbids every tool.",
    "placeholders": "{ORDER_NUMBER}, {ORDER_EMAIL} come from a web order the eval creates in its Testcontainers database; {FUTURE_DATE} is today + 7 days (yyyy-MM-dd, Bogota)."
